course: dictionary
lesson: 7444
title: Polystyrene: a light plastic
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Polystyrene is a light plastic. You can work out its meaning from the clues around it. «Polystyrene, the light white foam used in packing, is mostly trapped air bubbles.» The words light, foam and trapped air bubbles tell you what it is like.
explain: The sentence gives more clues. «It floats almost on top of the water» tells you it is light enough to float. «Bits of it pollute the sea for years» tells you it is harmful to nature. Polystyrene is a noun, so it names a thing.
explain: Polystyrene comes in different forms. The white kind is soft foam, but hard clear polystyrene is used for plastic cutlery and CD cases. Phrases like polystyrene cup or polystyrene packaging show you the kind of thing being described.
fact: Polystyrene is a light plastic.
fact: The common white kind is full of air bubbles and is used for packaging, cups and food boxes.
fact: Hard clear polystyrene is used for things like plastic cutlery and CD cases.
fact: In science, polystyrene is an insulator: it keeps heat in or out, and it floats.
fact: In environment lessons, polystyrene is hard to recycle and pollutes seas.
exercise: «Polystyrene, the light white foam used in packing, is mostly trapped air bubbles.» What is polystyrene mostly made of? | Liquid water | Solid stone | Sugar crystals | *Trapped air bubbles
exercise: Why does polystyrene float on water? | It is solid rock | *It is light and full of air bubbles | It is heavy and made of metal | It soaks up water like a sponge
exercise: Which of these is a polystyrene item? | A glass jar | A wooden spoon | *A white foam food box | A cotton towel
test: What does an insulator do in science? | It stops light from passing through | It turns water into ice | It makes sound louder | *It keeps heat in or out
test: Why is polystyrene a problem for the environment? | It is too heavy to move | It grows into trees in the sea | It makes the sea taste sweet | *It is hard to recycle and pollutes seas
exam: Ella says polystyrene is a metal. What is the right answer? | It is a type of liquid | *It is a light plastic | It is a heavy metal | It is a kind of wood
